# Case of the Pilfered Proof: only "a Detective you control" that is turned face up gets the counter (CR 701.40b, 205.3). Bot1's Case is out. Bot1's Forum Familiar (a Cat) is cast
# face down and turned up on turn 3; its own trigger puts a +1/+1 counter on it, and the Case adds none: a 2/2, not a 3/3. On turn 4 Bot2's Cryptic Coat cloaks a Novice Inspector,
# which Bot2 turns up as a Detective: Bot1's Case does not count it, and it is a 2/2 with the Coat's +1/+0, not a 3/3.

